// ── LAYER 1 · PULSE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Four-on-the-floor: the synthwave staple, and it doubles as the game's
// heartbeat. Hats sit OFF the beat — straight 8ths would plod; the offbeat is
// what gives the genre its lift.
//
// Playtest note (2026-08-02): "there's a snare or two that feel like they are
// in the middle of nowhere". They were: the open-hat turnaround fired on the
// 4th and 3rd-and-4th sixteenths of bars 4 and 8, which reads as a mistake
// rather than a fill because it lands off the backbeat with nothing leading
// into it. Fills now sit on the LAST beat of the phrase and build INTO the
// downbeat, which is what makes a fill parse as intentional.
setcps(0.5)
stack(
  s("bd*4").gain(0.50),                          // four on the floor
  s("~ cp ~ cp").gain(0.30),                     // backbeat on 2 and 4
  s("[~ hh]*4").gain(0.12).pan(sine.range(0.38, 0.62).fast(2)),

  // Turnaround: a 16th run on beat 4 of bars 4 and 8 — leading into the next
  // downbeat, never stranded mid-bar.
  s("<~ ~ ~ [~ ~ ~ [hh hh]] ~ ~ ~ [~ ~ [hh hh] [sn sn]]>").gain(0.20),

  // Open hat on the "and" of 4, every other bar: the classic lift.
  s("<~ [~ ~ ~ [~ ho]]>").gain(0.16),

  s("<cr ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~>").gain(0.20)             // marks the top of the loop
)
